  nonce: c9ec  # c9ec
  message: "SATISFIED (dev a9ff904f0e), on the standing ruling of 2026-08-31: close on the\nFILED ROW and file the residual.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, this item's own instance, through the production CLI on\nthe MERGED tree with a cleared cache (the run asserts its own \"No cached results\nfound\" line):\n\n  guacamole-client, host-secret-no-host-fs\n    BEFORE (dev e66ab343a3)   violated(3)\n      ... doc/licenses/generate-license-files.sh:1-1:file:file\n      ... guacamole-docker/build.d/020-download-drivers.sh:52-79:download_driver   <== FILED ROW\n      ... guacamole-docker/entrypoint.d/500-generate-tomcat-catalina-base.sh:1-1\n    AFTER  (dev a9ff904f0e)   violated(1)\n      ... doc/licenses/generate-license-files.sh:1-1:file:file\n\n  The filed row is GONE. The verdict stays `violated` on a surviving row, so\n  nothing was silenced into a false all-clear.\n\nTHE FIX, and it is not the one this item filed (root_cause corrected in place\nearlier today). A repo-wide index carries per-file assignment sets and the\n`source` graph, and the env-read discriminator asks \"assigned in any file joined\nto mine by source?\" -- BOTH directions, because bash is dynamically scoped:\ncilium's PROG is assigned at check-stable:19 and read inside the k8s-common.sh\nthat file sources, which a one-way rule would have missed.\n\nResolution is the half that was hard. Dynamic targets are dynamic in the PREFIX\nand literal in the TAIL (`source $TOOL_LIB_PATH/gitlib.sh`), so matching the\ntrailing literal component takes the followable population from 12 to 81 of 97\n(83.5%) with ZERO ambiguity on this cohort; a glob's trailing DIRECTORY\ncomponent recovers guacamole's container path without teaching bash about\nDockerfiles. Every branch fails closed.\n\nCOHORT, 16 repos, every repo cold in BOTH arms: 8 rows removed, 0 added, no\nverdict changed category, bash-sourced rows 32 -> 24. ALL 8 READ BACK against\nsource; each is a name genuinely assigned in a script joined by `source`.\nThe refuting case is a LIVE CONTROL and survives: the three vendored mvnw rows\nreading $HOME -- which the blunt whole-repo rule would delete -- are present in\nBOTH arms.\n\nRESIDUAL, filed as WI-<see sibling>: 13 of 97 source statements are a bare\n`$ENV_FILE` / `$f` / `$SCRIPT` with no binding this resolver reads, and 5 name a\ntail absent from the repo. Names assigned only through those remain classified\nas environment reads. That is the disclosed limit of this fix, not a claim that\nthe mechanism is extinct.\n\nALSO DISCLOSED, because it is a real choice rather than an oversight: EXECUTION\nORDER IS NOT MODELLED. The connected component is treated as one scope, exactly\nas INV-jurif's whole-file rule already ignores order within a file. guacamole's\nGUACAMOLE_HOME genuinely IS environmental where 100-generate-guacamole-home.sh:40\nreads it and locally assigned by line 63; both files are one scope here.\n\nArtifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pujob_bash_cross_source_08312026/ (README\nfirst -- it carries 8 traps, including why the mvnw rows are a control and why\narmN was restarted once)."  # c9ec
